    {
      "id": 95768,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-03-16T02:08:22.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You guys sure have a lot of cons in the midwest. &nbsp;Must not be a whole lot else to do out there. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/stuck_out_tongue.png?v=12\" title=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>You're absolutely right, of course.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Brock came by to say hi. Thanks, Brock!</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The game room was surprisingly well attended, and much larger than I'd expected. I figure there were chairs for 100 people in there and most of the afternoon they were all taken. I had no trouble finding people to play Sentinels. Had to turn some people away. Ok, it didn't help that we played a 90 minute game against La Capitan (but won!). The Whos Yer Gamers library also had two copies of Sentinels and they were both checked out most of the day, too.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:22:41.856Z",
